    /// <summary>
    /// Gives a key animation (as Player.setPoseAnimation takes it) a name, for every resource on this
    /// server: player.playAnimation(name) then plays it on the player's body (as
    /// Player.setPoseAnimation does) until stopAnimation or the next playAnimation, and
    /// playerAnimationEnd follows with 'stopped' or 'replaced'. playAnimation's `loop` option overrides
    /// the animation's own. Its effect events play on the player's body at their times, for the players
    /// within 250 m, again each loop, until it stops; the server does not play its sound events.
    /// Defining a name again replaces the animation. An animation defined by name may be up to 30000
    /// bytes as sent (a whole body, at most 32 keys and 32 joints): one longer than the player field's
    /// 2000 bytes goes to every player's game once by its name, players who join later too, and plays
    /// by that name. Throws a TypeError for a name that is not 1 to 48 letters, digits or _, and the
